\f1\b FOLDER: analyses\
\

\f0\b0 Folder with all files necessary to replicate the statistical analyses described in the experiment.
\f1\b \
\
raw_data_all_subjects.csv\
\

\f0\b0 Complete data for all three experimental conditions for all 40 participants in the study (n = 120 per participant). Data for pseudowords not used in the analyses and not included in the dataset, following the same guidelines for data sharing and data analyses as the original study. \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Raw data is not provided to ensure participant anonymity.\
\
Variables in the dataset are:
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\

\f0\b0  "word": the experimental stimuli        \
"participant": participant ID  \
"trial_n": order of presentation           \
"cond": the stimuli\'92s condition - iconic onomatopoeic words (onom), iconic non-onomatopoeic words 	(icon), non-iconic (nicon) and pseudo words (pseudo)             \
"correct_key": whether the correct response for the stimuli was pressing the key p or q\
"key_pressed": key pressed by participant      \
"answer": whether participant pressed the correct key (1) or not (0)             \
"rt": reaction time               \
"freq_corp_log": log-frequency (Soares et al. 2018)\
"freq_corp_abs_log": absolute frequency (Soares et al. 2018)\
"ort_nlet": length measured as the number of letters          \
"ort_neig_dl": orthographic levenshtein distance (Soares et al. 2018)      \
"ort_big_p_tk_med": mean bigram probability \
"icon_m": iconicity (Godoy, 2026)            \
"concreteness": concreteness (Santos et al. 2017)     \
"AoA": age of acquisition (Santos et al. 2017)          \
"POS": part-of-speech - nouns (n) and verbs (v) 
\f1\b \
\
\
